Kubernetes has become the backbone of modern cloud-native infrastructure. Whether you’re preparing for interviews or sharpening your skills, these are some of the most commonly asked Kubernetes questions in interviews:

🔹Core Concepts
1. What is Kubernetes and why do we use it?
2. Explain the difference between Pods, Deployments, and ReplicaSets.
3. How does a Kubernetes Service work?


🔹 Networking & Storage
4. What are the different types of Services in Kubernetes?
5. How does Ingress work in Kubernetes?
6. What are Persistent Volumes (PV) and Persistent Volume Claims (PVC)?

🔹 Scaling & Scheduling
7. How does Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) work?
8. What is the role of the Kubernetes Scheduler?

🔹 Security & Configurations
9. What are ConfigMaps and Secrets?
10. How do you secure a Kubernetes cluster?

🔹 Advanced Topics
11. Explain the difference between StatefulSets and Deployments.
12. How do you perform a rolling update vs a blue-green deployment in Kubernetes?
13. How do you debug a pod stuck in CrashLoopBackOff?
14. What’s the role of etcd in Kubernetes?
15. How does RBAC (Role-Based Access Control) work in Kubernetes?

💡 Pro tip: Don’t just memorize answers. Interviewers love real-world examples so talk about how you used Kubernetes in projects (deployments, scaling, monitoring, etc.).
